<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shibata Katsuie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1522–1583</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shibata Katsuie was a senior general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a>. He conquered Echizen and Kaga, crushing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikko-ikki">Ikko-ikki</a> of Kaga in 1580, and ruled from Kitanosho castle at modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukui">Fukui</a>. After Nobunaga's death he opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, was defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-shizugatake">Battle of Shizugatake</a> in 1583 and killed himself as his castle fell.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shibata-katsuie.jpg" alt="Shibata Katsuie" width="320" height="685" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shibata_Katsuie_large.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
